{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"wc -l /Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt70/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/capabilities/crud-and-state-machine.md && sed -n '1,240p' /Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt70/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/capabilities/crud-and-state-machine.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"wc -l /Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt70/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/capabilities/crud-and-state-machine.md && sed -n '1,240p' /Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt70/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/capabilities/crud-and-state-machine.md\"","aggregated_output":"      44 /Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt70/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/capabilities/crud-and-state-machine.md\n# CRUD and state machine\n\n> **TL;DR** — Owns: record CRUD projection and guarded state transitions (`state_machines[]` plus `transition_state` Actions). Read when: ordinary record mutation or a closed state graph is required. Never: generate a Handler for plain CRUD or an already expressible transition.\n\n## Problem and owner\nRuntime owns record query/detail/create/update/delete and guarded state transitions.\n\n## Supported model and Blueprint expression\nProject ordinary single-record behavior to Runtime record capability. Declare `state_machines[]` only when writes to one state field must follow a closed transition graph; invoke the transition through a published record Action with an idempotency key.\n\nChoose the owner from the required consequence — the full owner decision matrix is the single home in [behavior owner decision](behavior-owner-decision.md). State-machine-specific routing: plain single-record CRUD needs no state machine unless edge restriction is required; a guarded state-field change uses `state_machines[]` plus a Runtime `transition_state` Action; a state change that must commit atomically with other records uses one project-owned Handler Action whose state write still passes the state machine; human approval or waiting before a state change uses a Workflow whose Action node invokes the transition Action.\n\nA state machine requires a stable `key`, `object_key`, `field_key`, non-empty `states`, and `transitions`; use `name` for its business label and list only states intentionally allowed to have no outgoing edge in `terminal_states`. Every non-terminal state needs an outgoing transition. Every transition `from`/`to` must occur in `states`, and every state must match the state field's stored value domain. Within one state machine, each directed `from`/`to` edge may appear only once: a different `action_key` or `workflow_key` does not make the same edge distinct. Referenced `action_key` or `workflow_key` must name a declared resource.\n\n`action_key` and `workflow_key` on a transition are validated associations, not automatic side-effect execution. Runtime enforces the allowed edge when the record's state field changes, but a `transition_state` Action still needs the target state in its payload; a Workflow must explicitly contain the Action node that performs the change. `actions[].from_state` and `actions[].to_state` are retired fields. Do not invent transition `effects`, `patch`, or cross-object writes in the Blueprint state-machine entry; use an Action/Handler for the effect.\n\nThe exact invocation shape: the transition request body must carry the state field with the target value, e.g. `POST /objects/ticket/records/{id}/actions/ticket.close` with `{\"data\": {\"status\": \"closed\"}}`. With the payload, Runtime enforces the declared edges (an illegal from-state fails `backend.transition.invalid_transition`). Without the payload, the current Runtime fails closed with 400 `backend.action.transition_payload_required` (earlier platform builds silently returned 200 without changing state — still never treat a bare 200 as proof of the new state; assert the response record's state or read it back). Every acceptance journey and Handler that drives a transition must send the target state explicitly.\n\nOne behavior owns one concrete declared resource — `resource_key` resolution and the no-umbrella-key rule are owned by [behavior owner decision](behavior-owner-decision.md). If one requirement covers CRUD for several Objects, emit one behavior entry per Object:\n\n```json\n{\"key\":\"manage_gym_member\",\"trigger\":\"record_write\",\"scope\":\"single_record\",\"atomicity\":\"single_record\",\"failure_semantics\":\"reject_write\",\"owner\":\"runtime_crud\",\"resource_key\":\"gym_member\",\"rationale\":\"Runtime record CRUD\"}\n```\n\n## Reuse, extension, and prohibitions\nDo not generate a Handler for plain single-record CRUD or an already supported transition. Use project Actions only for semantics Runtime cannot express.\n\nRuntime Metadata also implements Object lifecycle modes `mutable`, `soft_delete_only`, `append_only`, and `immutable_after_state`, with `ledger_policy` available only for append-only Objects. The current Domain Blueprint `objects[]` contract does not expose `lifecycle_policy` or `ledger_policy`. Do not add those unknown fields and do not claim a Handler reproduces platform lifecycle enforcement. When the requirement needs enforced soft delete, append-only evidence, or immutability after a state, record a Domainry Plane/Blueprint capability-disclosure gap against the existing Runtime owner capability.\n\n## Examples\nCorrect guarded lifecycle:\n\n```json\n{\"key\":\"order_lifecycle\",\"name\":\"Order lifecycle\",\"object_key\":\"sales_order\",\"field_key\":\"status\",\"states\":[\"draft\",\"submitted\",\"approved\",\"rejected\"],\"terminal_states\":[\"approved\",\"rejected\"],\"transitions\":[{\"from\":\"draft\",\"to\":\"submitted\",\"action_key\":\"sales_order.submit\"},{\"from\":\"submitted\",\"to\":\"approved\",\"action_key\":\"sales_order.approve\"},{\"from\":\"submitted\",\"to\":\"rejected\",\"action_key\":\"sales_order.reject\"}]}\n```\n\nThe three Actions must be declared; invoking one must actually patch `status` to the matching target. Correct: update member phone through Runtime update. Wrong: `UpdateMemberHandler` only wraps one update. Wrong: expect `workflow_key:\"order_approval\"` on a transition to start that Workflow automatically. A booking plus capacity decrement in one transaction is a valid project-owned candidate.\n\n## Authority and limits\nBlueprint shape and closure: `internal/controlplane/blueprint/model/contract.go`, `internal/controlplane/blueprint/model/definition_action.go`, and `internal/controlplane/authoring/validation/behavior_validation.go`.\n\nRuntime transition execution: `internal/runtime/domain/record/validation/record_state_machine_validation.go`, `internal/runtime/application/action/action_catalog.go`, and `internal/runtime/application/action/action_system_operation_executor.go`.\n\nLifecycle capability and current Blueprint omission: `internal/runtime/domain/definition/model/definition_model.go`, `internal/runtime/domain/record/policy/record_lifecycle_policy.go`, and `internal/controlplane/blueprint/model/object_schema.go`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
