{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_74","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '/tmp/.*model.*validate|model validate --json.*tee|\\\"files\\\":[0-9]+,\\\"issue_count\\\"' /Users/tiger/Projects/domainry-skill-evals/runs/m1-crm-opt67-mysql-model-04/agent-model-opt67.jsonl | tail -80\"","aggregated_output":"365:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_192\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n -C 5 'plan.*artifact|plan.*receipt|model plan|plan result|evolution' /Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md /Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md | sed -n '1,300p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-39-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-40-## Requirement payload\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-41-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-42-A `requirement` item's `payload.requirement` carries the requirement statement plus its `behaviors[]` array of behavior-owner tuples (owner, resource_key, and the tuple fields defined in [behavior owner decision](capabilities/behavior-owner-decision.md)). An empty `behaviors` array is legal only when the payload also supplies a non-empty `no_executable_behavior_reason` string explaining why the requirement owns no executable behavior (for example, purely declarative authorization/navigation policy carried by roles, data permissions, and views). The field must be absent when `behaviors` is non-empty; `model validate` fails closed on both violations (`empty behaviors require a reason` / `ledger.requirement_incomplete`).\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-43-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md:44:For `object_sql_v1`, use exactly one project-owned SQL file named after the Report key instead of embedding a large escaped SQL string. Replace only the `sql` member with `\\\"sql_file\\\":\\\"backend/reports/<report-key>.sql\\\"`. `model validate|plan|apply` requires that exact canonical project-relative regular file, rejects symlinks/traversal and simultaneous `sql` + `sql_file`, normalizes line endings and a final newline, records its SHA-256 in the apply receipt, and embeds the normalized SQL into the existing published Runtime contract. `sql_file` is not a Runtime field or a query DSL; Runtime still receives `object_sql_v1.sql`, and `model export` may therefore emit the compatible inline form.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-45-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-46-## Commands\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-47-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-48-```text\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-49-\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" model preflight --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\"\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-50-\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" model validate --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\"\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md:51:\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" model plan     --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\"\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md:52:\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" model apply    --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\" --go-module-path <domain-qualified-module> [--environment <name> | --service <url>] [--allow-destructive] [--sync-only] [--evolution-audit-sha256 <emitted-sha256> --evolution-reason <reviewed-reason>]\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-53-\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" model export   --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\" [--force]\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-54-```\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-55-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-56-- `preflight` is the authoritative no-HTTP, local-read-only repair loop. It reuses the same model/SQL loader, strict item contract, Ledger graph, in-process authoring checks, and deterministic Runtime-manifest compiler as the formal path. It atomically replaces `.domainry/builder/disposable/model-preflight-result.json` for both `valid` and `repair_required`; stdout contains only `state`, `issue_count`, the project-relative artifact locator, SHA-256, and identity. A repair result exits non-zero. Read the artifact from the first Gate run and batch-repair it; do not rerun a failed Gate merely to obtain diagnostics and do not implement a bespoke `jq`/regex preflight. This local boundary does not claim live Plane, Runtime configuration, provider, database, or scenario checks.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-57-- `validate` parses every model file, enforces the item contract, and reports the pending plan counts without writing model/Ledger state.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-58-- `plan` additionally lists the exact item IDs classified as create, update, or delete.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md:59:- `apply` is the single release command: it converges the Ledger to the model files, gates on the aggregated metadata checklist, then chains live validation, signed publication, dependency resolution, backend materialization/evolution, and source finalization, stopping at the first failing stage. Every release apply resolves the dependency seed in staging before it installs files or writes a successful materialization receipt; a resolution failure stops closed and must be repaired before rerunning. For an existing Builder delivery change, the first run emits `evolution_review_required` plus an audit path and SHA-256. Inspect the immutable audit and rerun the same command with that exact emitted SHA-256 and a concrete review reason; never calculate or substitute the hash. After any other failure, repair the model files (or the reported stage input) and re-run the same command. stdout carries one compact summary; the complete receipt is written to `.domainry/builder/model-apply.json`. `--sync-only` stops after the Ledger sync and checklist for local iteration without a Domainry Plane target.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-60-- `export` bootstraps model files from the current Ledger (one file per module) for a project created before this workflow; it refuses to overwrite existing model files without `--force`.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-61-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-62-CAS identities, batch contexts, and Ledger journals are handled entirely inside the CLI. Never compute, copy, or supply a SHA-256 by hand, and never call Domainry Plane directly or reconstruct its request signing.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-63-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/backend-model.md-64-## Convergence and safety rules\\n--\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-38-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-39-Do not guess `--bind source` when no project source exists. After obtaining the Gate ID from `list`, invoke the same Gate runner with `attach --gate-id <gate-id> --status passed --evidence-type source_artifact --evidence-path docs/backend-requirements-prd.md --bind requirements`, or execute an applicable validator once with `run --gate-id <gate-id> --bind requirements -- <validator argv>`. Missing or empty PRD makes the binding unavailable. The requirements-only terminal “all in-scope requirements” Gate uses this closure and does not demand an implementation-coverage receipt; a change to any included evidence makes it stale. Every validation argv must itself fail closed: use no pipeline, or place `set -o pipefail`/`set -euo pipefail` inside the executed shell script before any pipeline; `tee` never turns an internal failure into a passing Gate.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-40-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-41-One Agent session corresponds to one TODO document and owns only `.domainry/development/<agent-session-id>.md`; never overwrite or update another session's document. A new session creates a new file even for related work and may reference prior session TODOs only as read-only handoff context.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-42-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md:43:The TODO is the only progress ledger. Do not keep a second execution plan. Append validation findings to this document, finish the reachable round, batch repairs, and revalidate until the finding inventory is empty. One artifact may support several items, but every Gate binds the artifact and exact fact proved. Changed evidence content or a bound source, requirements artifact, model/Blueprint, Runtime manifest, identity, or receipt-named artifact makes the Gate stale and requires current evidence. Keep evidence concise and link to large artifacts instead of pasting logs. The lightweight TODO checker only detects document consistency; it runs no build or Runtime work and is not a second completion authority, evidence database, or source-wide staleness system.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-44-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-45-Keep `assets/DEVELOPMENT_TODO.template.md` in the same dependency order as this guide; if the template order is wrong, correct and validate the template before using or releasing that Skill version — never work around a misordered template by executing later sections first.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-46-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-47-## Round discipline\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-48-\\n--\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-139-\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" contract capability-category --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\" --key <fixed-category-key>\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-140-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-141-# complete declarative model, inspection, and one-time legacy bootstrap\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-142-\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" model preflight --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\"\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-143-\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" model validate --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\"\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md:144:\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" model plan --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\"\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-145-\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" model export --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\"\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-146-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md:147:# the only release command; an existing delivery may require its emitted evolution review\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-148-\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" model apply --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\" --go-module-path <domain-qualified-module> --product-surfaces <business_workspace|consumer_portal|business_workspace,consumer_portal> [target] [--allow-destructive]\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md:149:\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" model apply --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\" --go-module-path <domain-qualified-module> --product-surfaces <same-reviewed-surfaces> [target] --evolution-audit-sha256 <emitted-sha256> --evolution-reason <reviewed-reason>\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-150-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-151-# approved source gaps\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-152-\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" project source prepare --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\"\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md:153:\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" action context --projection coding --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\" [--evolution-audit-sha256 <sha256>] <object.action>\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md:154:\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" action scaffold apply --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\" [--evolution-audit-sha256 <sha256>] ... <object.action>\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md:155:\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" action source apply --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\" [--evolution-audit-sha256 <sha256>] ... --input - <object.action>\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-156-\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" connector definition --json [target] <connector>\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-157-\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" connector context --projection coding --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\" <connector.provider>\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-158-\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" connector scaffold apply --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\" ... <connector.provider>\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-159-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-160-# source closure in this exact order before developer tests\\n--\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-221-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-222-| Decision class | Boundary | Required handling | Blocks model? |\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-223-| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-224-| `business_blocker` | Two or more concrete, mutually incompatible choices remain, and selecting one changes an explicitly required observable business result, authorization allow/deny result, amount/unit semantics, irreversible external effect, or business-state flow | Name the incompatible choices and the exact affected requirement/model items. Do not infer the choice from UI, fixtures, labels, legacy behavior, or implementation convenience; obtain a current user decision or accepted requirement evidence. | Yes, only for the smallest affected slice. |\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-225-| `contract_discovery` | Runtime-owned formal error code/category, canonical identifier or principal/context source, or the mapping of accepted facts to Action, Workflow, metadata, or another published capability | Discover it through the typed client, fixed capability categories, or another formal Runtime contract. If the formal contract is absent, record a Foundation/Runtime owner gap; do not turn it into a product question or invent a representation. | No. It may block affected implementation or acceptance after discovery fails, but not settled business modeling. |\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md:226:| `safe_implementation_decision` | A purely technical, reversible choice that preserves the accepted business invariant, including stable ordering with a unique tie-breaker, pagination maximum, index, internal resource key, and audit, idempotency, or concurrency mechanism | Use the published platform standard; otherwise record one deterministic, conservative safe default with its rationale and evolution path. | No. |\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-227-| `product_follow_up` | A product preference whose currently documented fallback does not change required observable results, permission, amount meaning, or business state in the accepted scope | Record the assumption, owner, fallback, excluded acceptance scope, and review trigger. Never relabel it `confirmed`. | No. |\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-228-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-229-Security and privacy omissions use a conservative `safe_implementation_decision`: least privilege, sensitive by default, and no export by default, with the evolvable assumption recorded. If an explicit requirement demands export or broader disclosure of a sensitive fact, that conflict is a `business_blocker` until its authorization and disclosure boundary is confirmed.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-230-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-231-Use these nonblocking defaults without inventing product rules:\\n--\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-310-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-311-```sh\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-312-\\\"$SKILL_ROOT/bin/domainry-development-todo-check.py\\\" --todo \\\"$TODO_PATH\\\" --expected-stage model\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-313-```\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-314-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md:315:The model files are the single backend authoring surface and the source of truth. Inspect the pending change set with `\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" model plan --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\"`; bootstrap an older project once with `\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" model export --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\"`. Do not edit `domain/**` or `.domainry/**` Ledger state by hand ([backend-model.md](backend-model.md)).\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-316-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-317-When the module inventories are complete, release the Blueprint once:\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-318-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-319-```text\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-320-\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" model apply --json --project \\\"$PROJECT_ROOT\\\" --go-module-path <domain-qualified-module> --product-surfaces <reviewed-surfaces> [one pinned explicit --environment or --service target]\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-321-```\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-322-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md:323:`model apply` is the only normal-development release command. The complete apply semantics — stage chaining, checklist gating, destructive refusal and `--allow-destructive`, rename = delete + create, receipt path, `--sync-only`, and the prohibition on direct Domainry Plane calls or split publish/materialize maintenance commands — are defined in [backend-model.md](backend-model.md). Always pass reviewed `--product-surfaces`; it is the backend-to-frontend integration boundary used by materialization, not authorization to generate or redesign page source. After a stage failure, repair the model files or reported input and rerun the same command. An existing delivery that returns `evolution_review_required` may rerun only with the emitted audit SHA-256 and reviewed reason.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-324-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-325-Backend materialization inside `model apply` installs backend templates, generated/source inputs, contracts, Runtime manifest, and Go dependencies. It must never create, modify, or delete `frontend/**`, including frontend paths contained in Project Source Seed.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-326-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-327-Backend materialization is not the local-composition compile closure. The project template may already call `composition.RuntimeOptions`, while `generated/composition/extensions.gen.go`, the Action registry, and the Connector registry remain owned by source finalization. Complete that closure only with `project source finalize`.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-328-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-329-### Implement and integrate\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-330-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-331-<a id=\\\"source-prepare-implementation-packet\\\"></a>\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-332-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md:333:- Run `\\\"$DOMAINRY_CLI\\\" project source prepare --json --project <project>` immediately after materialization. Treat the bounded envelope's Action key/path/state list as the Handler implementation inventory and retain the exact `.implementation_packet.path`, payload/file hashes, and delivery/materialization identity. The CLI atomically persists the complete content-addressed packet under managed `.domainry/builder/**`; never redirect stdout to create it and never use or invent `latest.json`. First inspect the envelope's small Action index, then use local `jq` for exactly one packet `actions[]` entry selected by `action_key` and only the referenced `documents[]` content selected by SHA. Never `cat` or print the complete packet, and do not issue one `action context` command per Action in the same installed batch. The command creates only missing canonical project-owned Handler/test skeletons, never replaces an existing file, and writes in bounded atomic batches. Use focused `action context` only for an isolated repair or an audit-bound pending evolution absent from the installed packet.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-334-- Compileability of a prepared skeleton proves only contract shape. Every prepared `*.not_implemented` result remains fail closed and must be replaced by accepted business behavior before source finalization can pass.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-335-- Obtain bounded coding context for approved source gaps.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-336-- Implement Handler, domain, Connector, and tests by module. Replace each generated placeholder test with typed non-nil Execution/capability stubs plus current output/effect assertions; retain separate hand-written nil/authorization robustness tests when they remain valuable.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-337-- Use generated typed capabilities and real data access.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-338-- Reject placeholders, empty success returns, and handlers that never use their capability set.\\n--\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-404-After the backend converges, read [evidence-levels.md](evidence-levels.md) and [verification.md](verification.md) completely and re-read [production-technical-gates.md](production-technical-gates.md). `project verify` and packaging prove `delivery_verified` structural/release closure, not `scenario_verified` real-data behavior. Keep verification and packaging as two independent development Gates and execute their exact `project verify --json` and `project package --json` commands separately; neither command receipt can close the other Gate. Run the complete verify check-and-evidence inventory specified in verification — source boundary, backend/frontend suites, checklist/live validation, verify + package, managed Runtime, acceptance denominator prepare/harness/check, authorization/data-scope/idempotency journeys, matrix consistency, long/dense cases, and cleanup. Guide-specific ordering rules:\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-405-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-406-- validate that the source-finalization receipt is still current; if source changes during repair, return to finalization before compiling or testing;\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-407-- confirm the persisted Action/permission and role/effective-menu matrices still match the restarted Runtime and accepted database.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-408-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md:409:After the matching managed Runtime is healthy, run `project acceptance prepare`, then execute the platform runner **first** with `project acceptance run --cases standard` and inspect its exact-set v2 result rows. Build business harness assertions on `assets/acceptance-harness-core.py` only for `state:\\\"not_passed\\\"` rows with `disposition:\\\"needs_business_harness\\\"`. Repair `blocked_dependency`, `blocked_platform`, `unsupported_runner`, `setup_failed`, `evidence_rejected`, or `runtime_failed` at the named owner before rerunning. Then run `project acceptance check`. Every assertion obtains its session through `harness.session_for_case(case)`, uses `ScenarioGraph` for isolated setup/dependencies, and applies `ReasonOracle` for the declared status/error/state/audit/positive-control reason; never select a user from a role name, create profile headers, or read an internal identity table. The denominator is CLI-owned and never hand-edited. After a model evolution, run `project acceptance stale-report` and re-record only reported `stale`/`missing` cases, never the full set. Prose, arbitrary hashed text, or a coverage percentage cannot replace the harness.\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-410-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-411-Record the whole verify round before repair. If any finding exists, return it to its model or implementation owner, repair the batch, and run verify again (Round discipline).\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-home-opt67/skills/domainry-builder-v1/references/development-guide.md-412-\\n/Users/tiger/.codex-run/domainry-plane-opt31c-262ca059-8283/codex-h